# Stacks & Services

## Core

The core stack provides foundational services required by other components.

Responsibilities include:

- Reverse proxy functionality
- Internal networking services
- Shared infrastructure components

Other stacks depend on services provided by this layer.

{{ core_table }}

## Apps

The apps stack contains user-facing self-hosted applications.

Applications are exposed through the reverse proxy and use the shared Docker networking infrastructure.

{{ apps_table }}

## Mail

The mail stack contains mail-related infrastructure.

Mail services integrate with the core networking layer and are exposed where required through the reverse proxy.

{{ mail_table }}

## Metrics

The metrics stack provides monitoring and visibility into the environment.

It operates independently from application workloads while connecting to the shared Docker networking layer.

{{ metrics_table }}